    "lawCode": "Amd §16-324, NYC Ad Cd",
    "lawSection": "New York City Administrative Code",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6139\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the administrative code of the city of New York, in\nrelation to requiring the sanitation department of the city of New\nYork to provide owners, lessees or person in charge of a premises at\nwhich a violation of the city solid waste disposal law is alleged to\nhave occurred with a photograph of the materials, condition or\nsituation constituting the violation\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nRequires the sanitation department of the city of New York to provide\na photograph of the materials, condition or the situation alleged to\nconstitute the violation.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a requirement to the administrative code of the city of\nNew York that would require violations to be accompanied by a\nphotograph taken by the enforcement agent of the condition on the\nproperty that led to the sanitation ticket's issuance.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis provision would enable residents to have a photo of the\nconditions on their property that lead to a New York city Department\nof Sanitation violation. It would also simplify the appeals process\nwith the Environmental Control Board. The administrative judge would\nhave a date stamped photograph to review while considering the\nproperty owner's appeal.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect ninety days after it shall have become a\nlaw.\n\n",
