    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6139A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act\nto amend the administrative code of the city of New York, in relation to\nrequiring the sanitation department of the city of New York to provide\nowners, lessees or person in charge of a premises at which a violation\nof the city solid waste disposal law is alleged to have occurred with a\nphotograph of the materials, condition or situation constituting the\nviolation\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nRequires a uniformed member of the sanitation department of the city\nof New York to provide a photograph of the materials, condition or\nthe situation alleged to constitute the violation.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a requirement to the administrative code of the city of\nNew York that would require violations to be accompanied by a\nphotograph taken by the enforcement agent of the condition on the\nproperty that led to the sanitation ticket's issuance.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis provision would enable residents to have a photo of the\nconditions on their property that lead to a New York city Department\nof Sanitation violation. It would also simplify the appeals process\nwith the Environmental control Board. The administrative judge would\nhave a date stamped photograph to review while considering the\nproperty owner's appeal.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n\n",
